    title: 'Tenerife with a Baby: A Stress-Free Guide for New Parents',
    excerpt:
      "Warm weather, short flights and easy logistics make Tenerife a great first trip with a baby. What to do, what to pack, and how to rent the bulky gear instead of flying with it.",
    date: '2026-10-29',
    author: 'Fun Zone Tenerife',
    category: 'Family',
    gradient: 'from-[#39ff14]/20 via-[#1a1a2e] to-[#0a0a0f]',
    readTime: '7 min read',
    content: [
      "Tenerife is one of the easiest destinations in Europe for a first trip with a baby. The weather is warm and predictable all year, the flight is manageable from most of Europe, there is no meaningful time difference to upset nap schedules, and the south of the island is flat, walkable and well equipped for families. With a little planning, a trip with a baby can be genuinely relaxing.",
      "Base yourself in the south for the calmest conditions. Los Cristianos and Costa Adeje have gently shelving, blue-flag beaches with calm water that are ideal for a baby's first paddle, plus wide promenades perfect for pram walks. Choose an aparthotel with a kitchenette and space for a nap, and you have the flexibility that makes travelling with a baby so much easier.",
      "There is still plenty to enjoy together. A short, calm <a href=\"/en/activities/whale-watching-tenerife\">whale watching trip</a> on a larger, stable boat works well (pick a shorter sailing and go on a calm morning), promenade strolls, gentle botanical gardens in the north, and simply easy beach mornings. Keep drives short and build the day around a midday nap, see more ideas on our <a href=\"/en/activities\">things to do in Tenerife</a> page.",
      "The biggest practical headache with a baby is the gear. Flying with a travel cot, a pushchair, a car seat and a high chair is expensive, bulky and stressful, and airlines regularly damage them. The simpler option is to rent baby equipment locally and have it waiting at your accommodation. We recommend <a href=\"https://babytravelrental.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">babytravelrental.com</a> for clean, safety-checked cots, strollers, car seats, high chairs and more, delivered across the south of Tenerife.",
      "A few last tips: the sun is strong even in winter, so pack high-factor cream, a hat and a pram sunshade; pharmacies are excellent and well stocked for anything you forget; and most restaurants are relaxed and welcoming with babies. Sort the logistics in advance, rent the gear, book a calm activity or two, and Tenerife with a baby becomes the easy, sunny break new parents actually need.",
    ],
